B.  Kolmogorov Complexity and Normalized Compression Distance

B.1  Plain and Conditional Kolmogorov Complexity

Fix a universal prefix Turing machine U.  For a finite binary string x,

K(x) = \min\{\,|p| : U(p)=x \,\}
\]  

is the Kolmogorov complexity of x.  For a pair of strings x,y,

K(x\mid y) = \min\{\,|p| : U(p,y)=x \,\}
\]  

is the conditional complexity.  The invariance theorem (Li & Vitányi 2019) states that K and K(\cdot\mid\cdot) are defined up to an additive constant independent of the chosen universal machine.

K is uncomputable.  For practical purposes we approximate it by the length of the output of a real‑world lossless compressor.

B.2  Approximation by Real‑World Compressors

Let \mathcal{C} be a set of standard compressors (e.g., LZMA, bzip2).  For a string x,

K_{\!C}(x) = |C(x)|\cdot 8 + \kappa,
\]  

where \kappa is a fixed overhead that accounts for the decompressor itself (≈ 67 kB for LZMA, per empirical measurements).  For strings shorter than 4 bytes a minimum floor k_{\min}=128 bits is enforced to avoid spurious ratios.

Conditional Kolmogorov complexity is approximated by the concatenation method

K_{\!C}(x\mid y) \approx K_{\!C}(y\;\|\;x) - K_{\!C}(y),
\]  

where \| denotes a distinguishable separator.  This method is motivated by the identity K(x\mid y) \approx K(yx) - K(y) that holds up to additive logarithmic corrections for the true Kolmogorov complexity.

B.3  Normalized Compression Distance (NCD)

Definition B.1 (Cilibrasi & Vitányi 2004)  For a compressor C the NCD between two strings x,y is

\operatorname{NCD}(x,y) = \frac{C(xy) - \min\{C(x),C(y)\}}{\max\{C(x),C(y)\}}.
\]  

NCD is a quasi‑universal similarity metric that approximates the normalized information distance.

B.4  Robust Supremum Over Compressors

To avoid sensitivity to the peculiarities of a single compressor, the main text employs a supreme over the set \mathcal{C}:

K_{\mathcal{C}}^*(x) = \sup_{C\in\mathcal{C}} K_{\!C}(x),\qquad
K_{\mathcal{C}}^*(x\mid y) = \sup_{C\in\mathcal{C}} \bigl( K_{\!C}(y\;\|\;x) - K_{\!C}(y) \bigr)_+.
\]  

This construction inherits the robustness of the NCD while preserving the theoretical interpretation.

